{#
  Beehiiv inline subscribe form — SINGLE SOURCE for every placement
  (/subscribe/, end of each article, homepage). Change the form here, not in
  three templates.

  The loader injects a cross-origin <iframe> from subscribe-forms.beehiiv.com
  into a wrapper div it creates itself, then sizes that wrapper from a
  postMessage the iframe sends back. Two consequences, both deliberate:

  1. NOTHING inside the form can be styled from our CSS — it is another origin.
     The button colour is set in Beehiiv's own Style tab, not here.
  2. If the resize handshake does not complete, the wrapper it creates stays at
     height:0 and the form is invisible. `.fd-subscribe-embed > div` below sets a
     min-height so a failed handshake still renders a usable form rather than a
     blank gap. Their inline height wins once it arrives, because an inline style
     beats a stylesheet rule — min-height only ever raises the floor.
#}
<div class="fd-subscribe-embed">
    <script async src="https://subscribe-forms.beehiiv.com/v3/loader.js" data-beehiiv-form="fabd7125-27ee-4bf4-933c-c278e180e97d"></script>
</div>
